From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:48:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Set the sleep LEDs and the lid wake under
 macOS

\_SI._SST of the H8 EC sets the indicators: on S3 the power button and
the dot of the logo pulse and the moon LED lights up, back to steady
light on wake. ACPICA (Linux) calls it around _PTS and _WAK; macOS does
not, and the LEDs stay as in S0 while the laptop sleeps.

Under macOS (ISDW), call _SST (3) at the end of _PTS for S3 and _SST (1)
at the start of _WAK. In _PTS, also arm the wake on lid opening with
_PSW of the lid (WKLD), as Linux does when it enables the lid as a
wakeup source: the Fn key already wakes the laptop under macOS, but
nothing shows that the lid is armed. Linux and Windows run the same
methods as before.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init. In
acpiexec, without _OSI ("Darwin") installed, _PTS (3) and _WAK (3)
leave the LED register (0x0c) and 0x32 of the EC at 0; with it, _PTS
(3) sets WKLD (0x32 = 0x04) and leaves the LEDs at 0xaa, the last value
of _SST (3), _WAK (3) at 0x8a, the last of _SST (1), and _PTS (4)
changes nothing.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
index 4297baf47e..bed1217185 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/acpi/platform.asl
@@ -2,6 +2,11 @@
 
 Method(_WAK,1)
 {
+	/* macOS does not call _SST: the indicators back to working */
+	If (\ISDW ()) {
+		\_SI._SST (1)
+	}
+
 	/* Wake the HKEY to init BT/WWAN */
 	\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.HKEY.WAKE (Arg0)
 
@@ -20,4 +25,14 @@ Method(_WAK,1)
 Method(_PTS,1)
 {
 	\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.RADI(0)
+
+	/*
+	 * Under macOS, before S3: the sleep indicators (power button and logo
+	 * pulsing, moon on), which macOS does not set with _SST, and the wake
+	 * on lid opening, which the other OSes enable with _PSW of the lid.
+	 */
+	If (Arg0 == 3 && \ISDW ()) {
+		\_SB.PCI0.LPCB.EC.LID._PSW (1)
+		\_SI._SST (3)
+	}
 }
